st 3 attempts in total, waiting `backoff * 2**attempt` between them: 0.5s, then 1s by default. You can set the base delay with the new constructor argument `backoff=0.5`.\n\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, the original `HTTPError` is raised.\n- Other HTTP errors (e.g. 500) are raised right away without retrying.\n- Network errors and timeouts (`URLError`, socket timeouts) are not retried either, since you only asked for 503.\n\nI tested it against a local HTTP server:\n\n| Scenario | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| No failures | success | 1 |\n| Two 503s, then OK | success | 3 |\n| Three 503s | `HTTPError 503` | 3 |\n| One 500 | `HTTPError 500` | 1 |\n\nThere are no tests in the repo, so I didn't add any.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 69558, "requests_cache_write": 143846, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7667376, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1677, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 5, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:36:23.951364+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 23.902, "t_checker_s": 2.391, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1691, "tokens_cache_read": 69558, "tokens_cache_write": 143846, "tokens_fresh": 1691, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 69558, "tokens_main_cache_write": 143846, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_output": 1677, "tokens_output": 1677, "t