e test against a real local HTTP server behaved as intended in all four cases I ran.\n\n**How it works:**\n- It makes at most 3 attempts in total. Before the 2nd and 3rd attempts it waits 0.5s, then 1s, doubling each time (`BACKOFF_BASE * 2**attempt`).\n- Only a 503 is retried. Any other error is raised right away, and so is a 503 on the last attempt, so callers still get the `HTTPError` as before.\n- Network errors and timeouts (`URLError`) are not retried; I kept strictly to 503 as asked.\n- I added an optional `sleep` argument to the constructor (defaults to `time.sleep`) so tests can skip the real waiting. Existing calls don't need to change.\n\n**Smoke test results** (status codes in the order the server returned them):\n\n| Server returns | Result | Requests made | Waits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | JSON returned | 3 | 0.5s, 1.0s |\n| 503, 503, 503 | `HTTPError 503` raised | 3 | 0.5s, 1.0s |\n| 500 | `HTTPError 500` raised | 1 | none |\n| 200 | JSON returned | 1 | none |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add a test file. That smoke test was a one-off and isn't saved in the repo.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 36280, "requests_cache_write": 142059, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7525589999999999, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1748, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial4", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 7, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:36:23.989513+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.343, "t_checker_s": 4.893, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_